id: pm-web-9sno
title: Add kanban board + full-text search data endpoints (contracts-driven)
description: ""
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[1]: sdk-capabilities
created_at: "2026-06-02T07:26:44.539Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T23:17:20.185Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T23:04:13.857Z"
author: codex
release: 2026.6.2
resolution: Work completed and released in 2026.6.2-1. Release attribution set explicitly so pm-changelog --respect-item-release files the entry under 2026.6.2-1 instead of the current release notes.
expected_result: "A closed item whose changelog entry appears under the 2026.6.2-1 heading it actually shipped in, leaving the current release notes untouched."
actual_result: "Before this closeout the item had remained in_progress with no activity since its work shipped, so the delivery was missing from the changelog while still being counted as open work in every fleet audit. Closing it with an explicit release attribution is what added the historical entry."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T23:17:12.354Z",claude-code,"Release attribution corrected to 2026.6.2 after review. The first attribution used the item's last-activity DATE, which is unsound: an item can be touched before the release that finally carried its code. Verified instead by tag containment — git tag --contains 175725a reports 2026.6.2 as the first release holding the implementation commit. Greptile caught this on PR #67 by noticing a historical release predating its implementation."
close_reason: "Retired as shipped: the kanban board and full-text search data endpoints, both present in src/board.ts and the /api/projects/:projectId/pm/board route today was completed and released in 2026.6.2-1, but the item was never closed and sat in progress ever since, inflating every fleet audit."
body: ""
